      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "What useEffect Is and the Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What it is and when it runs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useEffect(setup, deps?)` ==synchronizes== a component with an **external system**",
                "External = network, DOM API, timer, subscription",
                "{red:Not} a lifecycle hook"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Render",
                    "sub": "pure calc",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "sub": "DOM updated",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Paint",
                    "sub": "browser shows",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Effect",
                    "sub": "setup runs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "useEffect",
                "useLayoutEffect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Runs",
                  "after paint",
                  "before paint"
                ],
                [
                  "Blocks paint",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "fetch, subscribe",
                  "measure layout"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Mental model",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Think ==synchronize==, not 'on mount'",
                "Each render has its **own** effect closure",
                "It sees that render's props and state"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Caused by",
                "Put it in"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Component being displayed (fetch on show, subscribe, listener)",
                  "{green:Effect}"
                ],
                [
                  "User action (click, submit)",
                  "{blue:Event handler}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Shown on screen => ==effect==. User did something => ==handler==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why after paint?** So effects never block rendering",
                "**Layout vs effect?** `useLayoutEffect` runs pre-paint, `useEffect` after",
                "**componentDidMount?** No: it re-syncs whenever deps change"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dependency Arrays",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dependency Arrays",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Forms",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Deps",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "none",
                  "after **every** render"
                ],
                [
                  "`[]`",
                  "once after mount"
                ],
                [
                  "`[a, b]`",
                  "mount, then when a or b changes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each dep compared with ==Object.is==",
                "List **every reactive value** the effect reads: props, state, derived values",
                "Never silence `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Unstable Deps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Objects, arrays, functions made in the body are {red:new every render}",
                "As deps they re-fire the effect each time",
                "Fix: move {green:inside the effect}, {green:outside the component}, or {green:memoize}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Drop a Dep",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Functional updater `c => c + 1` removes state from deps",
                "Must not re-run? Read the latest value through a ==ref=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  const id = setInterval(() => setCount(c => c + 1), 1000);",
                "  return () => clearInterval(id);",
                "}, []);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Omit a dep?** Stale closure: the effect keeps an old value",
                "**Object in deps loops?** New identity each render, so effect sets state and repeats",
                "**How compared?** `Object.is` on each item"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cleanup Functions and Strict Mode",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cleanup Functions and Strict Mode",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Cleanup Basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Return a function from the effect to ==undo its setup==",
                "`removeEventListener`, `clearInterval`, unsubscribe, `abort()` a request"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  const id = setInterval(tick, 1000);",
                "  return () => clearInterval(id);",
                "}, []);"
              ],
              "note": "setup starts the timer, cleanup stops it"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Run Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Deps change",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Old cleanup",
                    "sub": "old values",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New effect",
                    "sub": "new values",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cleanup also runs on ==unmount=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Strict Mode (dev only)",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dev runs {orange:setup, cleanup, setup} to expose missing cleanup",
                "Result differs from one run (two timers, two connections)? Cleanup is {red:missing or wrong}",
                "Fix the ==cleanup==, not the double run"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**When does cleanup run?** Before the next effect (old values) and on unmount",
                "**Why twice in dev?** Strict Mode tests your cleanup",
                "**No cleanup on a subscription?** Leaked listeners, timers, connections"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fetching Data: Race Conditions, Loading and Error States",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Fetching Data: Race Conditions, Loading and Error States",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Race",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fast `id` change: ==older, slower response== lands last",
                "It {red:overwrites} the newer result"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Fixes",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Ignore flag==: cleanup sets `ignore = true`, `.then` skips `setData`",
                "==AbortController==: `signal` to fetch, `abort()` in cleanup"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  const c = new AbortController(); setLoading(true); setError(null);",
                "  fetch(url, { signal: c.signal })",
                "    .then(r => { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status); return r.json(); })",
                "    .then(setData)",
                "    .catch(e => { if (e.name !== 'AbortError') setError(e); })",
                "    .finally(() => { if (!c.signal.aborted) setLoading(false); });",
                "  return () => c.abort(); }, [url]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Request State",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Start: `loading` true, `error` null",
                "{red:fetch resolves} on 404/500: check `res.ok`",
                "`finally`: skip `setLoading(false)` if aborted"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Stale overwrite?** Ignore flag or abort in cleanup",
                "**fetch rejects on 500?** No, only on network failure",
                "**Why TanStack Query or SWR?** Caching, dedupe, races handled"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Avoiding Unnecessary Effects and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Avoiding Unnecessary Effects and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Skip the Effect",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Instead of an effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Derived data",
                  "Compute in render; `useMemo` if expensive"
                ],
                [
                  "Click, submit, POST",
                  "Do it in the ==event handler=="
                ],
                [
                  "Reset state on prop change",
                  "Give the component a ==key=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Effect + `setState` for derived data costs an {red:extra render}"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const full = first + ' ' + last;",
                "<Profile key={userId} id={userId} />"
              ],
              "note": "new key = fresh state"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useEffect(async () => ...)` returns a **Promise**, not a cleanup",
                "{red:Missing cleanup}: listeners, timers, requests leak",
                "Effect sets state it also depends on: ==infinite loop=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => {",
                "  async function load() { /* await ... */ }",
                "  load();",
                "}, []);"
              ],
              "note": "inner async function, then call it"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Three cases with no effect?** Derived data, user actions, prop-driven resets",
                "**Why not async?** It returns a Promise; React expects a cleanup function",
                "**Reset on prop change?** Give the component a `key`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useEffect Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useEffect Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Deps and cleanup",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Deps",
                "Runs"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "none",
                  "every render"
                ],
                [
                  "`[]`",
                  "mount only"
                ],
                [
                  "`[x]`",
                  "when x changes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "List ==every reactive value==; trust the lint rule",
                "Cleanup runs ==before the next effect== and on unmount",
                "Strict Mode dev double-run: ==result differs== from one run = bad cleanup"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fetch recipe",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "useEffect(() => { const c = new AbortController();",
                "setLoading(true); setError(null);",
                "fetch(url, { signal: c.signal })",
                "  .then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : Promise.reject(r.status))",
                "  .then(setData, e => e.name !== 'AbortError' && setError(e))",
                "  .finally(() => { if (!c.signal.aborted) setLoading(false); });",
                "return () => c.abort();",
                "}, [url]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Abort in cleanup (or an `ignore` flag)",
                "Check ==res.ok==: fetch won't reject on 404 or 500",
                "Loading false in `finally` ==unless aborted==",
                "State: loading, error, data"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Skip the effect",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Derived value",
                  "compute in render"
                ],
                [
                  "User action",
                  "event handler"
                ],
                [
                  "Reset on prop",
                  "`key`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Safe fetch on prop change?** Deps `[id]`, abort in cleanup, guard `finally`.",
                "**Wrong tool when?** Derived values, user actions, prop resets."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In development an effect logs `connected` twice in a row, with no `disconnected` between them. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The cleanup is missing or does not disconnect: the second connection leaks.",
                "Strict Mode runs setup, cleanup, setup, so a correct effect logs connected, disconnected, connected.",
                "Fix the cleanup: `return () => conn.disconnect()`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`useEffect(() => { fetch(url + id).then(r => r.json()).then(setData) }, [id])`. After `id` changes 1 to 2 quickly, the page shows user 1. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The slower response for 1 arrived last and overwrote the result for 2.",
                "Fix: pass an AbortController signal and abort in cleanup, or use an `ignore` flag."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Why does `useEffect(async () => { ... }, [])` break cleanup?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "An async function returns a Promise, which React cannot use as a cleanup function.",
                "Define an inner async function inside the effect and call it."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
